      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, 26 lb ≈ 12 kg. The standard dosing is **10–15 mg/kg per dose**, so at 12 kg that's **120–180 mg**, which equals **3.75–5.5 mL** of the 160mg/5mL concentration. A typical dose in this age group is about **5 mL (one 160 mg dose fits right in range)**, given every 4–6 hours, **no more than 4 doses in 24 hours**.\n\nTo give it: use the syringe that came with the medicine, dose in the back cheek, and go slow so he doesn't spit it out. Recheck his temp after 45–60 minutes — you should see it come down a degree or so, which is normal.",
