      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No — don't give another dose yet, and definitely **don't increase to 7 mL**. You waited only 2 hours; the minimum interval is **4 hours** between acetaminophen doses, and dosing above the calculated range adds risk without benefit. Fevers rarely \"break\" instantly — expect his temp to drop 1–2°F, not normalize, and sleepiness as the fever peaks is common. What matters more is **how he acts when awake**: if he's arousable, comforted, and改善ing, that's reassuring.\n\n**Take him to the ER now if**: he's hard to wake or won't stay awake, limp or unresponsive, has a stiff neck, trouble breathing, a rash that doesn't fade when pressed, or you can't get any fluids into him. Trust your gut — if \"super crazy\" means inconsolable or he genuinely seems wrong to you, get him seen tonight. (Note: I noticed \"改善\" slipped in — that's Chinese for \"improving.\")",
